                "username": "idgoktas"
              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "As world leaders prepare to gather in Ankara for the NATO Summit, President Erdoğan's assault on democratic freedoms is accelerating.\nOn the eve of the Summit, today marks the start of the decisive hearings in the trial of Istanbul Mayor @ekrem_imamoglu, widely regarded as President Erdoğan's leading political rival, who faces more than 2,000 years in prison. His prosecution has become a symbol of Türkiye's democratic backsliding. Our political family is in Istanbul today. MEP @NachoSAmor, the European Parliament's Rapporteur on Türkiye, is representing @TheProgressives and standing in solidarity with those defending democracy and the rule of law.\nMeanwhile, @eczozgurozel and other opposition leaders continue to face political and judicial pressure. Turkish journalists have been denied accreditation to cover the Summit. Most recently, comedian @idgoktas was arrested for exercising his freedom of expression.\nThe pattern is unmistakable: political opponents, journalists, artists and other independent voices are being systematically silenced. Such actions are a hallmark of authoritarianism.\nThe Party of European Socialists stands in unwavering solidarity with all those defending democracy, freedom and the rule of law in Türkiye. We will not remain silent."
        },
